From 5d66e719dbba00bcf89e896814bd79eb5a37e548 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Asius <dev@asius.ai>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 19:20:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: venus: program periodic H.264 and HEVC IDRs

The encoder registers V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_H264_I_PERIOD and stores its
value, but always programs an IDR period of zero. This makes only the first
I-frame an IDR frame and prevents a streaming decoder from joining or
recovering at later GOP boundaries.

Pass the configured H.264 period to firmware. Venus does not expose the HEVC
refresh-period control, so make every HEVC I-frame an IDR. This keeps raw HEVC
recordings independently decodable at GOP and segment boundaries.
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
index f7e8c4e55e12..60fbfc0d8d4b 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
@@ -765,7 +765,8 @@ static int venc_set_properties(struct venus_inst *inst)
 		 * n > 1 - every n-th I-frame will be IDR frame
 		 */
 		ptype = HFI_PROPERTY_CONFIG_VENC_IDR_PERIOD;
-		idrp.idr_period = 0;
+		idrp.idr_period = inst->fmt_cap->pixfmt == V4L2_PIX_FMT_H264 ?
+				    ctr->h264_i_period : 1;
 		ret = hfi_session_set_property(inst, ptype, &idrp);
 		if (ret)
 			return ret;
-- 
